# text = There was something crooked in her conscience after all ; for this very resolution seemed an acknowledgment that it was wrong to meet him at any time ; and yet she had brought herself to think her conduct quite innocent and proper , for although unknown to her father , and certain , even did he know it , to fail of obtaining his sanction , she esteemed her love-meetings with Mr . Carson as sure to end in her fathers good and happiness .
