# text = Wilson's thoughts soon returned to her husband , and their early married days pointing at one that hung against the wall said Mary counting with her finger Alice , who was standing near for the convenience of hearing , had caught much of this speech , and it was evident the subject had previously been discussed by the women , for she chimed in Mary ventured to say that she thought the Queen and Prince Albert could not make laws , but the answer was said Alice , who had not heard her sister's last burst of eloquence , and whose thoughts were still running on her nephew , and his various talents Mary went very red , and looked annoyed , although there was a secret spring of joy deep down in her heart , at hearing Jem so spoken of .
