# text = For , be it remembered , she had the innocence , or the ignorance , to believe his intentions honourable ; and he , feeling that at any price he must have her , only that he would obtain her as cheaply as he could , had never undeceived her ; while Sally Leadbitter laughed in her sleeve at them both , and wondered how it would all end -- whether Mary would gain her point of marriage , with her sly affectation of believing such to be Mr . Carson's intention in courting her .
