# text = She held one of the hands ( rapidly stiffening , even in her warm grasp ), and gently stroked the back of it , with the endearing caress she had used to all her children when young said she , looking up at her husband , and still smiling And , in truth , the lips , in the rest of death , did look as though they wore a smile , and the waving light of the unsnuffed candle almost made them seem to move said she to her youngest child , who knelt at her feet , trying to soothe her , by kissing her garments said nurse said the father , hastily interrupting her in dread of the distinct words which would tell of the changes of mortality said he to his wife said she , rising continued she , after she had bent down , and kissed the pale lips .
