# text = She looked at herself in the little glass which hung against the wall , and sadly shaking her head thought how easy were the duties of that Eden of innocence from which she was shut out ; how she would work , and toil , and starve , and die , if necessary , for a husband , a home -- for children -- but that thought she could not bear ; a little form rose up , stern in its innocence , from the witches' caldron of her imagination , and she rushed into action again .
