# text = She looked so piteously in Mary's face with her miserable eyes , that Mary felt her heart giving way , and , dreading the weakness of her powers , which the burst of crying she longed for would occasion , hastily changed the subject to Alice ; and Jane , in her heart , feeling that there was no sorrow like a mother's sorrow , replied Mary went upstairs ; partly because it is the etiquette in humble life to offer to friends a last opportunity of seeing the dying or the dead , while the same etiquette forbids a refusal of the invitation ; and partly because she longed to breathe , for an instant , the atmosphere of holy calm , which seemed ever to surround the pious , good old woman .
