# text = For you are aware that Alice , whose memory was clear and strong on all points in which her heart was interested , was lying in a manner senseless : that Jane Wilson was ( to use her own word , so expressive to a Lancashire ear ) " dazed "; that is to say , bewildered , lost in the confusion of terrifying and distressing thoughts ; incapable of concentrating her mind ; and at the best of times Will's proceedings were a matter of little importance to her ( or so she pretended ), she was so jealous of aught which distracted attention from her pearl of price , her only son Jem .
