# text = But then came in Margaret with her gentleness , like an angel of peace , so calm and reasonable , that both felt ashamed of their irritation , and tacitly left the decision to her ( only , by the way , I think Mary could never have submitted if it had gone against her , penitent and tearful as was her manner now to Job , the good old man who was helping her to work for Jem , although they differed as to the manner said Margaret to her grandfather , in a low tone Margaret had still , you see , little or no belief in Jem's innocence and besides , she thought if Mary saw Will , and heard herself from him that Jem had not been with him that Thursday night , it would in a measure break the force of the blow which was impending .
