# text = Sturgis alternately tended Mary , and wept over the violence of her illness , he listened to her ravings ; each sentence of which had its own peculiar meaning and reference , intelligible to his mind , till her words rose to the wild pitch of agony , that no one could alleviate , and he could bear it no longer , and stole , sick and miserable , downstairs , where Ben Sturgis thought it his duty to snore away in an arm-chair instead of his bed , under the idea that he should thus be more ready for active service , such as fetching the doctor to revisit his patient .
