# text = As he stood in the entrance to the foundry , awaiting Mr . Duncombe's leisure , many of those employed in the works passed him on their return from breakfast ; and , with one or two exceptions , without any acknowledgment of former acquaintance beyond a distant nod at the utmost said Jem to himself , with a bitter and indignant feeling rising in his throat Mr . Duncombe did not believe in Jem's guilt , in spite of the silence in which he again this day heard the imputation of it ; but he agreed that under the circumstances it was better he should leave the country Jem hung back from a confession with the awkwardness of a girl said Mr . Duncombe , smiling Jem felt that it was a relief to have this point settled ; and that he need no longer weigh reasons for and against his emigration .
