# text = But those who were admitted into his confidence were aware , that the wish that lay nearest to his heart was that none might suffer from the cause from which he had suffered ; that a perfect understanding , and complete confidence and love , might exist between masters and men ; that the truth might be recognised that the interests of one were the interests of all , and , as such , required the consideration and deliberation of all ; that hence it was most desirable to have educated workers , capable of judging , not mere machines of ignorant men : and to have them bound to their employers by the ties of respect and affection , not by mere money bargains alone ; in short , to acknowledge the Spirit of Christ as the regulating law between both parties .
